  "resolution": {
    "change": "patches/llvm-mos/0054-llvm-scavenger-save-range.patch",
    "causal_explanation": "findSurvivorBackwards validated a survivor at Pos, then moved Pos to earlier virtual-register instructions without validating the larger range. Crossing PH/PL made the selected status save unbalanced while X/Y remained live. Recheck canSaveScavengerRegister at each proposed extension and retain the last feasible range. Targets using the default always-true hook keep their search behavior.",
    "trigger_check": "The identical original scal-to-vec3-O0.ll fails with the recorded status-save abort on preserved llc-vector-enabled and passes with the generic scavenger change. The separately constructed 54-line MIR reproduces that exact baseline abort in both a16/xy16 and checks PHP/PLP nested within PHA/PLA. Executing the same MIR after PEI on bsnes-jg yields bytes 6,6,7,1 in default/a16/xy16, consuming the preserved carry and both index registers. Both original C inputs pass all four formerly failing configurations using the installed compiler.",
